// Rule 119's card, at declaration level. A KPI card informs; it is the
// read-only indicator the rule describes, with no call to action inside it.
//
// This one declares that it acts. The promise and the intent contradict each
// other, and the operator is left to poke the interface to learn which is true
// -- which is Rule 119's own reason: an interface learned by poking is an
// interface that was never read.
//
// Expected: ROLE_ACTS_WITHOUT_CONSEQUENCE

DEFINE INTERACTION revenue_card (
  SATISFIES [READ],
  ROLE inert
)

DEFINE INTERACTION overdue_card (
  SATISFIES [SCAN, ACT],
  ALWAYS_REACHABLE [UNDO],
  ROLE inert
)
